A drained share joins a queue without bringing the release forward.
The kernel would look for it too late, and the share wait past the tick its account filled;
a drained share that waits fills no earlier than the release.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a drained share's account fills before the release

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -208,7 +208,6 @@ static void share_settle(struct share *s)
     }
     if (s->drained && s->queue != NULL && s->budget != 0 &&
         tick_before(sched_ticks + share_fill(s, s->balance), nearest_release)) {
-        nearest_release = sched_ticks + share_fill(s, s->balance);
     }
 }
 
